---
// Required closing disclaimer, in v4's plain goodbye voice — a product built on
// honesty owes you its limits in the same voice as its strengths.
---

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="limits-h">
  <div class="shell max-w-3xl">
    <h2 id="limits-h" class="rise mt-4 text-[clamp(1.7rem,3.5vw,2.5rem)]">
      It won’t pretend to be your doctor.
    </h2>
    <div class="rise mt-7 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      <p>
        Healthee isn’t a medical device, and it won’t diagnose you. Everything here comes from a
        consumer band on your wrist, shown with how sure it is — an estimate, never a verdict.
      </p>
      <p>
        It’s not a stand-in for real care. If something in your numbers looks worth worrying about,
        it’ll say so plainly — and tell you to see a real doctor. It turns down medical, diagnosis,
        and emergency questions on purpose — not because a lawyer said so, but because guessing at
        your health would break the one promise the whole thing is built on.
      </p>
      <p class="text-ink">
        We tell you this the same way we tell you everything else: plainly. It’s still being built,
        out in the open, one honest piece at a time — and when it’s ready, this is where you’ll find
        it. <span class="font-semibold">Watch this space.</span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
